<% day_word = ->(days) { days == 1 ? 'day' : 'days' } -%>
Hello <%= @user.login %>,

VPS <%= @vps.id %> <%= @vps.hostname %> has repeatedly triggered our resource protection system.

<%= @incident_type_label %>
<% if [@warning_period_days, @stop_period_days, @incident_count_7d, @incident_count_30d].all? { |value| value.is_a?(Integer) && value >= 0 } &&
      [@warning_limit, @stop_limit].all? { |value| value.is_a?(Integer) && value.positive? } -%>
Period | Incidents | Limit | Action
<%= @warning_period_days %> <%= day_word.call(@warning_period_days) %> | <%= @incident_count_7d %> | <%= @warning_limit %> | Warning
<%= @stop_period_days %> <%= day_word.call(@stop_period_days) %> | <%= @incident_count_30d %> | <%= @stop_limit %> | VPS stop
<% end -%>

This load disrupts other VPSes on the same node.
Please check memory usage and service settings. Reducing the number of worker
processes in your web server or application may help.

<% if @stop_enforced -%>
If this happens again, the VPS may be stopped.
<% end -%>

Please resolve the issue.

<% incidents = if @contributor_snapshot_available
                 Array(@contributing_incidents).select { |incident| incident[:available] }
               elsif @trigger_incident && @trigger_incident[:available]
                 [@trigger_incident]
               else
                 []
               end -%>
<% if incidents.any? -%>
Incidents<% if @contributor_snapshot_available %> (<%= incidents.length %>/<%= @contributing_incident_count %>)<% end %>:

<% incidents.each do |incident| -%>
  #<%= incident[:id] %><% if incident[:detected_at] %> | <%= local_time(incident[:detected_at], '%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z') %><% end %> | <%= incident[:subject].to_s.gsub(/[[:cntrl:]\u2028\u2029]/, ' ') %>
<% if incident[:url] -%>
    <%= incident[:url] %>
<% end -%>
<% end -%>

<% end -%>
<% if @incident_history_url -%>
Incident history in vpsAdmin:

  <%= @incident_history_url %>

<% end -%>
Best regards,

vpsAdmin
